# Extra exclusions for Shift+F3 only — the home-wide search.
#
# This is layered ON TOP of ~/.config/fd/ignore, never instead of it: that file
# is the one list fd and ripgrep follow for ordinary searching, and nothing
# here should change what `fd` or `rg` do at a prompt. These paths are excluded
# only when the finder is asked to search all of $HOME.
#
# Why it exists: without it, a home-wide search does not finish. Measured on
# 2026-09-01, `fd -t f -H . ~` had not enumerated $HOME after two minutes and
# was still running; with these paths excluded it returns 402,970 files in
# 2.2s, and ripgrep answers a query in about 15s. ~/Library is the bulk of it —
# application support, caches, containers and the iCloud mirror — and none of
# it is a thing anybody is looking for when they search their own machine.
#
# The test for adding a line: would a hit here ever be one you wanted? If it is
# somebody else's data about your data, it belongs in this file.
Library/
.Trash/
.cache/
.local/share/
Applications/
.npm/
.cargo/registry/
.rustup/
.gradle/
.m2/
Pictures/
Movies/
Music/
